1
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:08,780
When I was in fifth grade, I pointed
a gun at a man and killed him.

2
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:11,560
Let's go, bitch!

3
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:13,545
Fill it up or you get it, too!

4
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:18,780
Give me the money now or
I'm gonna kill her next!

5
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:20,440
I swear I'll do it!

6
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:36,017
You little give it back you brat!

7
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:37,017
Let go.

8
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:38,760
Let go of my gun!

9
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:11,620
I pulled the trigger three times.

10
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:28,860
Ever since that day,

11
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:32,500
if I saw a gun on TV or
even a picture of one,

12
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:36,900
it would trigger my PTSD and
send me into a panic attack.

13
00:01:47,940 --> 00:01:53,740
Mets didn't help counseling didn't help
nothing helped me get rid of my phobia

14
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:50,220
I will help you to create something.

15
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:57,537
I will drop on my eyes.

16
00:02:57,620 --> 00:02:59,177
I will put my love on your heart.

17
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:04,957
I will never know that I will never know.

18
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:10,137
I will never know that I will never know.

19
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:15,857
But I'm not even happy with the world.

20
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:17,077
I'm not happy with the future.

21
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:22,097
I'm happy with the

22
00:03:22,180 --> 00:03:24,277
eyes of my eyes.

23
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:27,097
I'm happy with the red
eyes of my eyes. I'm

24
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:33,957
happy with the sadness.

25
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:38,540
I'm happy with the sound of my eyes.

26
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:54,437
I thought if I got as far
away from home as I could.

27
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,977
To this high school in Tokyo.

28
00:03:56,060 --> 00:03:57,697
I'd get better somehow.

29
00:03:57,780 --> 00:03:59,500
But nothing changed.

30
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:01,230
Bang.

31
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:02,497
Looking back.

32
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:06,557
I don't have any regrets pulling
that trigger to protect my mom.

33
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:08,037
But the thing is.

34
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:12,296
I'm not strong enough to convince
myself it was the best choice either.

35
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:16,860
Despite being so screwed up, I
did make one friend in Tokyo.

36
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:20,436
He was the one who got me
into playing Gungale online.

37
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:22,200
Kyoji Shinkawa.

38
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:25,420
But I've been totally left behind.

39
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:27,077
That is so not true.

40
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:31,572
In the last qualifier, you made it all
the way to the semifinals, remember?

41
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:33,550
Whatever.

42
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:36,577
An AGI build only gets you so far in GGO.

43
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:38,240
A good gun helps, too.

44
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:40,801
I spent points on the wrong stat.

45
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:43,037
Don't get so down about that stuff.

46
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:43,950
Sign up for B .O .B.

47
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:45,175
and see what happens.

48
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:48,260
Nah, no point. I'd just die.

49
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,400
Uh-oh, it's late.

50
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:52,820
Sorry, I have to get going now.

51
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:57,920
Thanks for the tea. And thanks.

52
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:00,860
I mean, thank you for saving me.

53
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:02,580
You were pretty cool.

54
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:06,386
I wish I could always
be there to protect you.

55
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:10,500
Hey, uh, if you want, I can
walk you home every day.

56
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,380
I mean, if you want.

57
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:15,337
Oh, no, no, that's okay.

58
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:16,460
I'll be fine.

59
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:18,878
It's the only way I'll get stronger.

60
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:23,598
At the time, I was so focused on
taking care of me and getting better,

61
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:26,427
I didn't notice Kyoji's
true feelings for me.

62
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,140
In GGO,

63
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:35,820
I became Xenot, the Sniper,

64
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:39,512
and I made it my mission to
take on the strongest players.

65
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:47,990
Next!

66
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:27,241
Bullets are flying, and
he's got the guts to save.

67
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:30,580
Maybe I will, too, when I kill him.

68
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:07,047
I thought the stronger
Xenon got in the game,

69
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:09,494
the stronger I'd get in the real world.

70
00:07:09,780 --> 00:07:15,080
I believed it with every fiber in me, so
I took on all comers with my Hecate II.

71
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:18,650
You're dead.

72
00:07:56,340 --> 00:07:58,046
We're the governor's offices.

73
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:02,917
I was on my way over to sign up
for the prelims for the third

74
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:07,059
Bullet of Bullets tourney when I
met a player calling herself Kirito.

75
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:13,240
Turns out she was a he and insisted
on using a sword in a game of guns.

76
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:14,937
Boy, did he piss me off.

77
00:08:15,020 --> 00:08:15,902
You're kidding!

78
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:17,060
No way!

79
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:19,860
You're a guy with that avatar?

80
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,180
Why, you—

81
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:37,000
Even though he pissed me off, I could
tell he was fighting his own demons.

82
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:39,800
Just like I was.

83
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:09,442
He won't even know what hit him.

84
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:17,820
Does he think he can dodge
my bullet at this range?

85
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:25,020
Does he even want to?

86
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:33,100
Don't, don't screw with me!

87
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:01,630
Fight me!

88
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:02,960
Come on, fight!

89
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:05,728
Or maybe you think I'm
not worth the effort!

90
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:07,400
You got it all wrong.

91
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:09,935
All I want is to compete in the final.

92
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,139
There's no reason to fight anymore.

93
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:15,917
Then go on and shoot yourself
and get it over with!

94
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,471
To you, it's just a game.

95
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:18,940
Just one stupid match.

96
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:22,857
That's all it is to
you, is that it? A game?

97
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:26,280
Well, just cause you feel
that way doesn't mean I do!

98
00:10:31,740 --> 00:10:34,681
Xenon, give me a chance
to make it right with you.

99
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:36,996
Let me give you the fight I promised.

100
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:03,360
Okay, get set.

101
00:11:39,380 --> 00:11:40,800
No way!

102
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,220
That's impossible!

103
00:11:57,820 --> 00:12:02,057
You knew where I was
aiming but how how'd you

104
00:12:02,140 --> 00:12:04,717
know I was going for
your leg I knew because

105
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:06,697
I Could see your eye
through the lens of your

106
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:11,540
scope that's how he
predicted my bullet's path

107
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:18,100
That's amazing that kind of
power is way beyond any vr game

108
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:23,720
If you're so strong you can do that,
why'd you look so afraid before?

109
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:26,270
You're wrong.

110
00:12:26,353 --> 00:12:27,359
It's not strength.

111
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:28,815
All it is is a skill.

112
00:12:30,340 --> 00:12:31,437
No, it's not.

113
00:12:31,520 --> 00:12:35,226
Technique isn't enough to cut a
bullet from my Hecatee in half.

114
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:37,180
You and I both know that.

115
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:40,517
It takes strength and all I
want to know is how to get it.

116
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:41,617
It's what I...

117
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:44,220
It's what I'm here to figure out.

118
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:46,970
Listen,

119
00:12:47,053 --> 00:12:49,977
could you shoot a player
in here if you knew

120
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:52,884
in the real world that
player would die from it?

121
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:55,613
And what if you had to kill that player?

122
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:59,177
Because if you didn't, you or
someone you love would die instead.

123
00:12:59,260 --> 00:13:02,613
If you had that power, could
you still pull that trigger?

124
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:14,857
When death gun drew down on me, all
the hope i'd put into sinon's strength?

125
00:13:14,940 --> 00:13:16,240
was shattered.

126
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:21,520
I type 54, Black Star.

127
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,140
It's the gun.

128
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:36,230
Why?

129
00:13:36,313 --> 00:13:37,143
Why here?

130
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:39,320
Why does he have that gun?

131
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:50,780
Okay, then who's next?

132
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:55,200
I got a feeling that right
now in the real world,

133
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:57,497
Death Gun's partner's in your place.

134
00:13:57,580 --> 00:14:01,874
He's watching the live stream, waiting
for when you get shot by that gun.

135
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:03,339
It's just a hunch.

136
00:14:09,060 --> 00:14:09,890
No!

137
00:14:10,580 --> 00:14:12,620
No, not that! Oh, God!

138
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:34,266
Until Death Gun shoots you, The guy in
your place isn't gonna do anything, okay?

139
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:37,729
That's the rule they
set up for themselves.

140
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:41,452
But if you log out now and
wake up with his partner there,

141
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,600
he'll kill you.

142
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:56,500
Tell me you got a plan.

143
00:14:57,760 --> 00:14:59,760
We're going to take out Death Gun.

144
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:06,097
Please, Hecate.

145
00:15:06,180 --> 00:15:08,800
I'm weak and I need your strength.

146
00:15:09,260 --> 00:15:12,780
The strength to stand up
for myself and move on.

147
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:19,430
Concentrate.

148
00:15:19,513 --> 00:15:21,220
Home in on his drive to kill.

149
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:32,410
Uh!

150
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:38,370
Uh!

151
00:15:44,620 --> 00:15:48,800
Get it out!

152
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:06,340
Gatia.

153
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:57,920
Damn it, he's tough.

154
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:02,400
If I can slow him down, in
one second's all I need!

155
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:07,177
Right now, Kirito's trying to get
that closure he was talking about.

156
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:12,025
He's confronting his demons from SAO by
taking on the person who represents them.

157
00:17:12,320 --> 00:17:13,150
Death Gun.

158
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:16,880
And the reason he can
isn't cause he's strong.

159
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:21,297
It's cause he accepts what he did,
even though it still tears him up.

160
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:24,060
And he's still trying
to move on, despite it!

161
00:17:28,020 --> 00:17:29,920
I've got to do something. Think!

162
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:40,310
Kirito!

163
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,677
Xenon's distracting him
with her bullet line.

164
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:50,407
She's got him in her sights,

165
00:17:50,620 --> 00:17:53,817
using all her skill and spirit
to keep it trained on him.

166
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:55,660
It's like a phantom bullet!

167
00:17:57,120 --> 00:17:58,857
One last attack.

168
00:17:58,940 --> 00:18:01,560
I can't waste this chance!

169
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:43,900
Oh!

170
00:19:08,380 --> 00:19:09,317
Fool.

171
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:11,560
It's not over yet.

172
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:13,837
You can't stop me.

173
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:15,540
He'll find you.

174
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:19,640
And he'll...

175
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:25,560
No, Zaza.

176
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:26,800
You're done.

177
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:29,080
And we'll find your partner, too.

178
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:32,377
He won't kill anyone anymore.

179
00:19:32,460 --> 00:19:33,880
Laughing Coffin's dead.

180
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:06,940
It's over.

181
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:08,370
Yeah.

182
00:20:11,700 --> 00:20:13,120
My name is Shino.

183
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:14,520
Shino Asura.

184
00:20:17,340 --> 00:20:21,046
I guess now we should probably
get this tourney over with, huh?

185
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:23,520
Yeah, we should.

186
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:26,230
There.

187
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:45,980
I love you, Asuna.

188
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:50,237
I thought once I got to be the
strongest player in Gungale Online,

189
00:20:50,320 --> 00:20:53,496
it'd somehow cancel out my
weakness in the real world.

190
00:21:02,340 --> 00:21:04,340
I couldn't have been more wrong.

191
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:06,120
Run, Sinon!

192
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:20,340
I realized Sinon and Shino were the same.

193
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:21,660
They were me.

194
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:23,334
Come on, are you okay?

195
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:32,318
I know I won't get better overnight.

196
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:34,957
It's going to be a long time before I can

197
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:37,628
come to grips with the
memory of what I did.

198
00:21:43,080 --> 00:21:47,900
Even so, little by
little, I will get better.

199
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:51,660
It's okay.

200
00:21:54,840 --> 00:21:58,840
This world isn't that scary anymore.

201
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:02,080
It's pretty nice, actually?

202
00:22:51,880 --> 00:22:54,060
Oh?

203
00:23:35,820 --> 00:23:38,060
Next time, the Queen of the Lake.
